Description:

Sieve "redirect" can now add a DKIM2 Message-Instance header field
documenting the header fields the script changed, so that a later hop can
sign the forwarded message without breaking its chain of custody.


Documentation:

lib/imapoptions/dkim2_message_instance, and
draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec-06 for the header field itself.


Config changes:

dkim2_message_instance (new, ENUM, default "off")


Upgrade instructions:

Nothing to do.  The feature is off by default; Cyrus never signs, so it is
only worth turning on where something downstream adds the DKIM2-Signature.
Use "verify" unless every step between the incoming SMTP conversation and
Sieve is known to leave signed header fields alone.


GitHub issue:

None.
